{
 "kind": "junie",
 "command": "junie",
 "source": "agents/junie.transcript.jsonl (research): permission turn lines 49-61, ask turn lines 33-39, session/load answer line 68 and its replay lines 65-67 (before) and 73-74 (after). The rest was recorded for this adapter against Junie 26.11.3 with a scripted fake LiteLLM model (scratchpad junie/tools/fake.py, junie/rec/): initialize and session/new (with brave_mode) and the tool turn from rec/http.jsonl (the program's tool over an HTTP MCP server, the filter picking it, permission Yes; the reply's number replaced by $TOOL, and the completed update's text, which Junie fills with a one-sentence summary its model writes rather than the tool's output, replaced by a summary of the same kind since the fake model wrote `x`), set_config_option from rec/safe.jsonl, ask_other from rec/ask_custom.jsonl (two questions, the first answered in its `_custom` field), reject from rec/dirs_off.jsonl (a file creation refused with No; the turn goes on), bad key from rec/anth.jsonl (a real Anthropic call with a fake key: the turn ends cancelled with no reply). Composed: hello (the tool turn's title and final answer chunk with its text changed). Each turn's `available_commands_update` and `config_option_update` notifications are left out (weft reads neither); Junie's own `_auth/status_update` notifications are kept. initialize, session/new (models cut to the first four of the first group) and set_config_option were recorded again for real against Junie 26.11.3 on a Junie token, through weft's agent server (`--model gemini-3.6-flash`, its answer's model currentValue `v1:12:jetbrains-ai:gemini-3.6-flash`); the token's account had no JetBrains AI subscription, so the real prompt ended `cancelled` with 0 tokens and its log said 403 NO_LICENSE, and no real turn could be recorded.",
